detector,special,constant,1.0,0.0,,,,,,0,,,"sentinel material for detector/absorber faces in the ray tracer; loader must accept it, n_complex returns 1+0j","Sentinel row (not a physical material); n=1 k=0 placeholder so detector faces do not refract/absorb via Fresnel terms",,,,,,,
calcite_o,oxide,sellmeier,0.96464345,1.82831454,0.73358749,0.0194325203,120,1e-08,,2710,0.204,2.172,"ordinary ray, uniaxial crystal; Ghosh's native 2-term form (n^2-1=A+B1*lam^2/(lam^2-C1)+B2*lam^2/(lam^2-C2)) mapped into this schema's 3-term Sellmeier via B3=A,C3=1e-8 um^2 (loader requires Ci>0 so a true C3=0 identity is not allowed; lam^2/(lam^2-1e-8)~=1 to <1e-7 relative error over lam=0.2-2um, i.e. numerically exact); technically a carbonate not an oxide -- grouped under 'oxide' class for taxonomy simplicity (no dedicated carbonate class in schema, same precedent as mgf2 fluoride row); verified n(590nm)=1.65830 vs target 1.658","Ghosh 1999, Opt. Commun. 163, 95-102 (dispersion-equation coefficients for calcite and quartz); coefficients per refractiveindex.info (shelf=main, book=CaCO3, page=Ghosh-o)",,,,,,,
calcite_e,oxide,sellmeier,0.82427830,0.14429128,0.35859695,0.0106689543,120,1e-08,,2710,0.204,2.172,"extraordinary ray, uniaxial crystal (negative uniaxial: n_e<n_o, pairs with calcite_o above); same exact Ghosh-2-term-to-3-term mapping as calcite_o (B3=A,C3=1e-8 um^2, see calcite_o note); grouped under 'oxide' class for taxonomy simplicity per mgf2 precedent; verified n(590nm)=1.48611 vs target 1.486","Ghosh 1999, Opt. Commun. 163, 95-102; coefficients per refractiveindex.info (shelf=main, book=CaCO3, page=Ghosh-e)",,,,,,,
